<h3>Can I change an invoice after issuing it?</h3>
<p>
  No, and that's on purpose: issued invoices are legal documents. If it's unpaid, an admin can void
  it and you issue a corrected one. The voided number stays visible so there are no gaps.
</p>

<h3>A customer paid part of an invoice. What do I do?</h3>
<p>
  Record the amount you received. The invoice shows <em>Partially paid</em>
  and the remaining balance;
  record more payments until it's paid.
</p>

<h3>I recorded a payment by mistake.</h3>
<p>
  Open the invoice and remove the payment (hover it and click the bin). The invoice status and your
  books are corrected automatically.
</p>

<h3>Why does my balance sheet show “Current earnings”?</h3>
<p>
  That's your profit to date. It belongs to the owners, so it sits in equity until your accountant
  closes the year.
</p>

<h3>Can I use more than one currency?</h3>
<p>
  Each workspace has one base currency today and documents are issued in it. Multi-currency is on the
  roadmap.
</p>

<h3>How do I save an invoice or report as PDF?</h3>
<p>Click <strong>Print / PDF</strong>, then choose <em>Save as PDF</em> as the printer.</p>

<h3>Someone from Zippiker support needs to look at my account.</h3>
<p>
  Our support staff can open your workspace to help you. Every such visit is recorded in our audit
  log, and they'll always tell you beforehand.
</p>

<h3>Something is still unclear</h3>
<p>
  Write to <a href="mailto:support@zippiker.com">support@zippiker.com</a>
  and tell us which page you were
  on. We read everything.
</p>
